                <pb facs="0349" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4997: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Prince</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-22T11:00:00+01:00">August 22, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 22—10:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. [Paraphrase]. Yesterday in private audience King Alexander personally
                    requested me to send the following message to President Hoover regarding the
                    moratorium proposal: [End paraphrase]. <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I ask President Hoover and his advisers to consider the lamentable
                            situation in which Yugoslavia would be placed in view of her existing
                            financial obligations if our country should lose 888,000,000 dinars
                            during the coming year according to the terms of the moratorium. I
                            therefore earnestly request President Hoover to do his utmost to help us
                            in our present dilemma of which I can see no other solution.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
